                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "5e6fab5b-2273-3192-8000-eeffd5dada68",
                        "entry_id": "7e713234-5e5e-3e9b-9115-f0bfe0bbecf6",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Wortzeichen, das die Form eines Bindestrichs hat und dazu verwendet wird, einen Wortteil, der nicht mehr in eine Zeile passt, abzutrennen und in die folgende Zeile zu verschieben."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "56e4b72f-be71-4fb4-b17d-c538285677b9",
                                "sense_id": "5e6fab5b-2273-3192-8000-eeffd5dada68",
                                "text": "Ein Trennungsstrich soll gemäß den Trennungsregeln gesetzt werden."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "18381182-d177-4ac1-9673-a6a3c15e3124",
                                "sense_id": "5e6fab5b-2273-3192-8000-eeffd5dada68",
                                "text": "Der Trennungsstrich dient dem Schriftbild eines Textes, indem er es ermöglicht, bei zu langen Wörtern einen einheitlichen Rand einzuhalten."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "7e57a0d8-63ab-4840-8bd4-8cca93706443",
                                "sense_id": "5e6fab5b-2273-3192-8000-eeffd5dada68",
                                "text": "Der Trennungsstrich zeigt an, dass die Wortteile, die er trennt, in einem Wort zusammengehören."
                            }
                        ],
                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "51a8a931-d9ef-3494-a859-d106a7ab948c",
                        "entry_id": "7e713234-5e5e-3e9b-9115-f0bfe0bbecf6",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Abgrenzung gegenüber etwas Unerwünschtem"
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "figurative"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "c19f9e9d-c7e1-4fe7-8659-6571a9fe821f",
                                "sense_id": "51a8a931-d9ef-3494-a859-d106a7ab948c",
                                "text": "Nach diesen Vorkommnissen sahen wir uns gezwungen, einen Trennungsstrich zu ziehen und uns nicht mehr an dem Plan zu beteiligen."
                            }
                        ],
                        "sense_index_json": "\"2\""
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "b919e903-759d-4c22-b514-d7cbcd7b866b",
                        "source_entry_id": "7e713234-5e5e-3e9b-9115-f0bfe0bbecf6",
                        "source_sense_id": "5e6fab5b-2273-3192-8000-eeffd5dada68",
                        "target_lang_word": "hyphen",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "hyphen",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "b318cea7-15b3-3d4a-8565-b31fad261823",
                                        "entry_id": "2160f5a2-191f-3086-9e2f-376e7152a451",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The symbol \\\"‐\\\", typically used to join two or more words to form a compound term, or to indicate that a word has been split at the end of a line."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d7683d01-c96a-4836-bd2b-b5efe8f62d31",
                                                "sense_id": "b318cea7-15b3-3d4a-8565-b31fad261823",
                                                "text": "As the proud owner of my very own hyphen in a lovingly crafted surname, I have an especial soft spot for this most confusing of punctuation marks."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "6f81b127-7781-3719-b694-1758702267b0",
                                        "entry_id": "2160f5a2-191f-3086-9e2f-376e7152a451",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Something which links two things of greater significance than itself."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "figuratively"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "417a5fe2-4525-4b6e-9144-a2e76f67d9b2",
                                                "sense_id": "6f81b127-7781-3719-b694-1758702267b0",
                                                "text": "Cunliffe and Karunanayake (2013) developed Fine's notion to introduce potential hyphen spaces that are deeply implicated and reciprocally influential in relationships between researchers and the researched."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "b2e60e67-3a73-378e-8497-2bff7439856f",
                                        "entry_id": "2160f5a2-191f-3086-9e2f-376e7152a451",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Something which links two things of greater significance than itself.",
                                            "An enclosed walkway or passage that connects two buildings."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "figuratively"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9e31c897-079d-42f0-9a0f-e5f6a520cfb6",
                                                "sense_id": "b2e60e67-3a73-378e-8497-2bff7439856f",
                                                "text": "The hyphens were added, joining the structures into one building, which now measures just over two hundred feet long."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "47e1d7e2-d9ac-481a-aa23-25eb19dbfcd6",
                                                "sense_id": "b2e60e67-3a73-378e-8497-2bff7439856f",
                                                "text": "Construction details for the hyphens, or \"connecting wings\" as they were called by the contractors, were included in the contractors' specifications, as follows:"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "cd7e6d9c-eb44-4e3e-9368-356c681e2855",
                                                "sense_id": "b2e60e67-3a73-378e-8497-2bff7439856f",
                                                "text": "Those were the “hyphens,” the passageways that connected the wings of the mansion to its center."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "2a51aeb5-2096-3429-9e73-9a36fac6203d",
                                        "entry_id": "2160f5a2-191f-3086-9e2f-376e7152a451",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Someone who belongs to a marginalized subgroup, and can therefore described by a hyphenated term, such as \\\"German-American\\\", \\\"female-academic\\\", etc."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "581d4d52-c758-41c7-b937-76227a1f7693",
                                                "sense_id": "2a51aeb5-2096-3429-9e73-9a36fac6203d",
                                                "text": "Tab has been kept on quite a number of members who rapturously applauded when that part of the message in which the hyphens were attacked was read by the President."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d6b2ac64-0bf9-4c91-b08b-c70e3d06fed5",
                                                "sense_id": "2a51aeb5-2096-3429-9e73-9a36fac6203d",
                                                "text": "Sign language interpreters fascinate me because their cultural space, \"working the hyphens\" as Michelle Fine (1994) would call it, and performing in the kind of hybrid third space that Homi Bhabha (1994) has written about resonates often with my own \"hard-of-hearing\" doubly hyphenated existence in both deaf and hearing worlds."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "726a9a95-1adb-44a5-8a26-ec88f1b8c202",
                                                "sense_id": "2a51aeb5-2096-3429-9e73-9a36fac6203d",
                                                "text": "A leading Republican paper also had, on the eve of the convention, focused attention on this issue by remarking that Hughes was “designated by the Hyphens as their agent to punish Mr. Wilson for his partial refusal to comply with Potsdam orders."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "hyphen",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c4d91480-cce4-371d-8eed-5250fc4d61ef",
                                        "entry_id": "d6dc8d65-582c-3488-a85a-4beb8ff311ee",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To separate or punctuate with a hyphen; to hyphenate."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "dated",
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "hyphen",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d5bed3d9-d198-33dc-8ac9-fb5789276e7f",
                                        "entry_id": "aad3dc38-95ef-3b43-ab09-51dbcc71d289",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Used to emphasize the coordinating function usually indicated by the punctuation \\\"-\\\"."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "81a0db43-25bf-4ae9-9fe8-128874bc4275",
                                                "sense_id": "d5bed3d9-d198-33dc-8ac9-fb5789276e7f",
                                                "text": "You are sitting at the wrong table, if I may be so bold, among the misguided who believe in the mass murder of mentalities, otherwise known as the liberal arts hyphen vocational training hyphen education."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a6a4c582-9019-453e-b28b-2acb9730c4e8",
                                                "sense_id": "d5bed3d9-d198-33dc-8ac9-fb5789276e7f",
                                                "text": "Ax was now a Hollywood hyphenated man. An actor hyphen director hyphen writer."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c19ed819-cd97-4924-a379-f83e72f2421a",
                                                "sense_id": "d5bed3d9-d198-33dc-8ac9-fb5789276e7f",
                                                "text": "He described himself as a poet-composer and actually said the word hyphen when he did so: \"I'm a poet hyphen composer."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "42cf41a7-aa47-46f8-a10b-ef1e148ac698",
                                                "sense_id": "d5bed3d9-d198-33dc-8ac9-fb5789276e7f",
                                                "text": "He is an actor (hyphen) writer (hyphen) director. In the fifth year of the series Alan Alda added another title to his growing list — that of creative consultant."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c7ba0306-fd83-4544-b81f-6a93c89681c9",
                                                "sense_id": "d5bed3d9-d198-33dc-8ac9-fb5789276e7f",
                                                "text": "One reason he has avoided reading legal thrillers is that “they seem really to have been written by lawyer-hyphen-authors.”"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "d7f31161-fb17-404e-9647-fc7dc5745b2b",
                        "source_entry_id": "7e713234-5e5e-3e9b-9115-f0bfe0bbecf6",
                        "source_sense_id": "5e6fab5b-2273-3192-8000-eeffd5dada68",
                        "target_lang_word": "tiret",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "tiret",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "97dfa81b-5c60-3e9f-af58-4ed339e6748b",
                                        "entry_id": "7eb74c70-0a98-3f80-a6af-68a107645408",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Petit trait (—) qui sert à indiquer un nouvel interlocuteur dans un dialogue, à séparer une phrase ou une partie de phrase comme le font les parenthèses, ou à énumérer des éléments dans une liste."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "211c5537-8053-4375-8a3e-788276a0638e",
                                                "sense_id": "97dfa81b-5c60-3e9f-af58-4ed339e6748b",
                                                "text": "S’il y avait des dialogues, encore. Tu parles ! Des pages bourrées de lignes comprimées entre des marges minuscules, de noirs paragraphes entassés les uns sur les autres, et, par-ci par-là, la charité d’un dialogue – un tiret, comme une oasis, qui indique qu’un personnage parle à un autre personnage. Mais l’autre ne lui répond pas. Suit un bloc de douze pages !"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1bcc16fa-d2fd-4d46-a9e7-3eba04af28a6",
                                                "sense_id": "97dfa81b-5c60-3e9f-af58-4ed339e6748b",
                                                "text": "Vous aurez noté à ce point de l’intrigue que la saynète est dépourvue de dialogues, qu’on reconnaît d’ordinaire au fait que les tirets se succèdent au gré des tours de parole.\nIl aurait dû y avoir quelque chose comme :\n– Enchanté, monsieur.\nPuis :\n– Très bien, je n’y manquerai pas.\nMais il n’y a manifestement pas."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fe76a56e-e623-4842-aa72-9d74e5cc076d",
                                                "sense_id": "97dfa81b-5c60-3e9f-af58-4ed339e6748b",
                                                "text": "Dans le langage courant, nous appelons « tiret » tout trait horizontal. Sur le clavier français du PC, le caractère de soulignement (_) est ainsi traduit par « tiret bas », voire « tiret du 8 », tandis que celui qui cohabite avec le 6 et s'emploie comme trait d'union (-) devient de façon similaire le « tiret du 6 ». Or les véritables tirets typographiques, dont le rôle est de ponctuer, sont absents du clavier. Il s'agit du tiret long (—), de moins en moins utilisé hormis dans les dialogues, et du tiret moyen (–), initialement réservé aux énumérations […]."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "de1c753c-92f3-357e-9c7a-c3a5d4705239",
                                        "entry_id": "7eb74c70-0a98-3f80-a6af-68a107645408",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Petit morceau de parchemin coupé en long et tortillé, servant à enfiler et à attacher des papiers ensemble."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "dated"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
